<!-- 

(acronym) 

element = things like header, h1,h2, p, title, etc...
id = specific for one element, like the word itself, an i'd
class = multiple elements
span = span can be used inline, its like extended use for what you do, its still in the same line as the paragraph
section = word itself, groups elements like a section in a class
div - divides into each section
article = will work independently even if you moved them to other
strong = turns into bold (strong importance)
em = turns into italic (emphasized text)
nav = navigation/buttons
h1 - h6 varies is size
header = top as its word says it but at the top-left corner when you first make one
footer = as its word says 
nav = as its word says

-->

<!-- 

color - can be accesed with either the name of it, the rgb value, hexidecimal values, or hsl values.
font-size measurement can be pixels(px) or em(standard)
em - think it as a standard    example: 1.1em = 110%
-->

<!-- 

font- family: chooses which specific font style or family to use (Arial, Times New Roman, or cursive)
font-size: how big or small the text appears on the screen (px, %, em)
font-weight: thick or heavy the lines of the letters are (normal, bold)  ex. 400   700
font-style: Changes angle or posture of the text (normal, italic)

-->

<!-- 

border-style: create box (solid, dashed, dotted, double, groove, ridge, inset, outset)
border-width: thickness (px,  )
border-color: simply color (name, rbg, hsl, hexidecimal)
boder-radius: rounds the corner of the border, higher number in pixels, more rounded, up to 20px
border: 3px solid purple; - shorthand syntax
border-botoom: simply just bottom part
border-right: simply just right side
border-left: simply just left side

-->